  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian response through provision of multisectoral life-saving assistanceHumanitarian response through provision of multisectoral life-saving assistance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Sudan continues to grapple with the effects of protracted conflict, economic instability, and environmental challenges such as floods and droughts. These factors have exacerbated health inequities, increased mental health burdens, and led to large-scale internal displacement. Vulnerable populations, including internally displaced persons (IDPs), returnees, and communities affected by conflict, require coordinated interventions to address their pressing needs. With this funding, IOM seeks to contribute to evidence-based decision-making amongst humanitarian partners and address vulnerability among affected persons by implementing an integrated health, Mental Health and Psychosocial Support (MHPSS), and Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) programme that is both responsive and data-driven.</narrative>
  </description>
